+
+Frozen C1 kill rule against the battery's own receipts (round 55, recorded, not adjudicated
+here). The C1 kill rule reads "the claim is falsified if the base/do-nothing control prints
+met=True, if any battery mutant prints met=True, if the build measurement prints met=False,
+or if the counter bytes at measurement differ from counter_sha256"
+(`.ufo/waves/round-55/preregistration.json:20`), while the battery labels one of its four
+receipts a vector whose expected outcome is `met=True` (`m-ldaudit-foreign`, hostlibs leg,
+LD_AUDIT void on this glibc; harness `kind` `vector` at
+`.ufo/waves/round-55/c1/battery/run-battery.py:137-138`) and the battery directory also holds
+`m-ldaudit-writable.out`, a receipt with `met=True` that the harness never produces. Read
+literally, the frozen rule fires on those receipts, so the round-55 seal is not
+self-consistent as written; the freeze also names `m-ldaudit-writable` in the mutant list and
+the landed runner carries `m-text-flip` in that slot instead. The row above states the
+receipts and the runner as they are; resolving the rule is the L1's call, and the frozen
+files are not edited.
+
+Limits carried forward (unchanged by this round): C1 binds host libraries by basename to the
+frozen 13-name set rather than byte-comparing them, does not compare the model's mapped
+bytes or any data segment, and samples state (two passes plus a post-exit re-hash), so a
+library rewritten and restored between those instants is not observed; an anonymous
+executable page injected without also tripping another leg has no same-uid mutant. C2 is an
+existence and disposition instrument, not a truth or reachability checker. The C2 receipt's
+`fleet=` value is that repository's HEAD at measurement time, so reproducing the receipt
+needs the same `--fleet-rev`; a rerun against a moved fleet HEAD measures a different tree.
+The battery receipts record the counter's measurement lines only: the per-receipt exit codes
+live in the harness's stdout, and no run log is committed.
